    "markdown": "---\ntitle: Electricity\naudience: CBSE Class 10\nsubject: Science\nchapter_number: 11\nchapter_slug: electricity\nstatus: published\nsource_textbook: textbooks/science/extracted/jesc111.pdf\n---\n\n# Chapter 11: Electricity\n\n## Published platform flow\n\n1. 11.1-11.3 current, potential difference, and circuit diagrams\n2. 11.4-11.5 Ohm's law, resistance, and resistivity\n3. 11.6.1 resistors in series\n4. 11.6.2 resistors in parallel\n5. 11.7 heating effect\n6. 11.8 electric power and energy\n7. All NCERT examples, in-text questions, exercises, and revision\n8. Board-exam practice\n9. 20-question mastery quiz\n\n## Accuracy decisions\n\n- Ammeter and voltmeter placement is explicitly guarded.\n- Both possible graph orientations are distinguished.\n- Series/parallel derivations, circuit design, and combined-network numericals\n  are worked step by step.\n- Power and energy calculations retain SI and commercial units.\n- Figures 11.1-11.3 and 11.6-11.7 use exact NCERT source schematics with\n  accessible HTML label keys.\n\n",
