    "markdown": "---\ntitle: Our Environment\naudience: CBSE Class 10\nsubject: Science\nchapter_number: 13\nchapter_slug: our-environment\nstatus: published\nsource_textbook: textbooks/science/extracted/jesc113.pdf\n---\n\n# Chapter 13: Our Environment\n\n## Published platform flow\n\n1. 13.1 ecosystem components\n2. 13.1.1 food chains, food webs, trophic levels, and energy flow\n3. biological magnification\n4. 13.2.1 ozone layer\n5. 13.2.2 managing garbage\n6. All NCERT in-text questions, exercises, and revision\n7. Board-exam practice\n8. 20-question mastery quiz\n\n## Accuracy decisions\n\n- Food-chain arrows run from food to consumer.\n- The roughly 1% solar capture and 10% trophic transfer statements are kept\n  distinct.\n- Energy decreases upward while persistent pollutant concentration can\n  increase upward.\n- Ozone formation, UV protection, CFC damage, and waste management are\n  answered in cause-effect form.\n- All important figure labels are readable in accessible HTML keys.\n\n",
